{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Commutative Ring.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Commutative Ring.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"commutative ring commutative ring","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Commutative Ring.md","fileName":"Commutative Ring.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Commutative Ring","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ring and Ideal Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Ring Identity","Ideal","Quotient Ring","Module","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Commutative Ring.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Commutative Ring.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"commutative ring commutative ring","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Commutative Ring.md","fileName":"Commutative Ring.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Commutative Ring","heading":"Commutative Ring","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A commutative ring is a set with addition and multiplication in which addition forms an abelian group, multiplication is associative, multiplication distributes over addition, and the order of factors does not change a product. The source assumes rings also have a [[Ring Identity]].\n\nCommutativity lets left and right multiplication be treated uniformly. [[Ideal]]s, [[Quotient Ring]]s, and [[Module]]s are the principal structures used to study such a ring.\n\nThe modern-algebra text introduces commutativity as an additional ring property rather than including it in the base definition. This distinction allows the same ring framework to include noncommutative examples while supporting the commutative ideal and field theory used later.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Ring Identity","Ideal","Quotient Ring","Module","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Commutative Ring.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Commutative Ring.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"commutative ring commutative ring","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Commutative Ring.md","fileName":"Commutative Ring.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Commutative Ring","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Ring Identity","Ideal","Quotient Ring","Module","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}